{153}{One thing at a time, then.}{}{5}{}{1}{ }
{154}{One thing first.}{}{-4}{}{1}{ }
{160}{Even on Sundays. Sometimes I fall asleep standing up. Then he bangs a piece of iron on the bench. I hear it when I'm trying to sleep, too.}{Even on Sundays. Sometimes I fall asleep standing up. Then he bangs a piece of iron on the bench. I hear it when I'm trying to sleep, too.}{}{}{0}{ }
{161}{You need rest and proper food.}{}{5}{}{200}{ }
{162}{You need food. Sleep.}{}{-4}{}{200}{ }
{163}{I will come back.}{}{5}{}{0}{ }
{164}{I come back.}{}{-4}{}{0}{ }
{180}{Eleven. I think. Mr Appleby says I'm old enough to be useful. I start when the clock strikes six. I finish when it strikes ten at night. Sixteen hours. I counted.}{Eleven. I think. Mr Appleby says I'm old enough to be useful. I start when the clock strikes six. I finish when it strikes ten at night. Sixteen hours. I counted.}{}{}{0}{ }
{181}{Every day?}{}{5}{}{160}{ }
